From 722626e6cc0ac80176216d554e8019562d522c72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LUgABeEEE <LUgABeEEE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:06:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(gateway): add an opt-in static-asset cache as a
 local patch

Upstream withdrew the three-group cache in #267 (reverted by #327) because the
API and history groups had no reachable HTTP route: session lists and history
are frames on /api/remote.mux. This local patch keeps only the group that has a
real route - /plugins and /assets - and leaves the rest out on purpose.

- contentCacheAssetTtlMs (0 = off), contentCacheAssetPaths (/plugins and
  /assets only), contentCacheMaxBytes, contentCacheMaxEntries.
- Every hit revalidates with If-None-Match; only a 304 replays the stored body
  (Age, X-DSH-Mobile-Cache). Browser responses keep Cache-Control: no-store.
- Writes, uploads, event streams, range requests, Set-Cookie responses and
  oversized bodies are never cached, and a write never clears the group.
- Gateway-owned /mobile-access routes are answered locally and never reach the
  proxy, so they are not in the default path list.

Not ready for upstream submission as-is: it still needs real-device hit and
saving measurements. See patches/README.md.
